    "deep_input_sha256": "7444310f6e9f16337a70cf45980260809b8601a91adb667f8a9618ba62414f51",
    "notes": [
      "Only four greedy Q4 drafters select these costs; C1, C2, fixed mode and Q8 choices remain unchanged. Sampled and mixed cohorts retain private decisions and RNG consumption.",
      "Shallow controls use a fresh server, one warmed measured round, context 4096 and no prompt-cache hits. All candidate outputs match C1 AR.",
      "The d32K controls use context 36864 and the same cached-prefix/pp2048/tg128 continuation. Each request caches 32552 of 34563 prompt tokens. Prefill and decode interleave as in normal HTTP serving; this is not a synchronized steady-state decode-only measurement.",
      "Four middle complete GPU cycles per width provide the offline cost estimate. These instrumented runs are calibration, not headline throughput.",
      "Maintained full-model checks pass, including exact sampled/mixed C2/C4 proposal lengths, IDs, probabilities, private RNG and restored state. Nix release and canonical PR checks passed.",
      "The 1.5% deep-context timing difference is provisional from one pair; prefill timings are comparable. The larger shallow gains are 26.9% and 13.0%."
    ]
  },
